# No commits, no comments

## Git

- Never create commits, stage files for commit, or push.
- The user commits. Do not offer to commit unless they explicitly ask.

## Comments

- Do not add comments to new or edited code.
- Do not leave leftover explanatory, narrating, or AI-style comments.
- Prefer clear names and structure over comments.
- Only keep a comment if it is required for a non-obvious constraint (legal, protocol, or a deliberate workaround) and the user already has that style in the file — still prefer zero comments by default.
